// Syllabus — Thermodynamics & Statistical Mechanics (curated course; see collection.js for references)
//
// Sources consulted (research pass, Oct 2026):
//   Schroeder, An Introduction to Thermal Physics — section-level TOC (refs '§x.y' verified):
//     https://physics.weber.edu/thermal/contents.html
//   Kardar, Statistical Physics of Particles — chapter/section order via MIT 8.333 lecture notes:
//     https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-333-statistical-mechanics-i-statistical-mechanics-of-particles-fall-2013/pages/lecture-notes/
//   Tong, Lectures on Statistical Physics (Cambridge Part II) — chapter contents (refs chapter-level):
//     https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/
//   Callen, Thermodynamics and an Introduction to Thermostatistics — chapter structure (refs chapter-level)
//   Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_laws_in_science (thermodynamics),
//     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_paradoxes (thermodynamics: Gibbs, Loschmidt, Maxwell’s demon)
// Gaps filled after comparison: Dalton’s law, Newton’s law of cooling, Rankine cycle and adiabatic
//   demagnetization (Schroeder §4.3–4.4), BBGKY hierarchy (Kardar §3.3), Fokker–Planck equation,
//   Bohr–van Leeuwen theorem, Landau diamagnetism and Pauli paramagnetism (Tong ch. 3),
//   Kramers–Wannier duality, Lee–Yang theorem and Landau–Ginzburg theory (Tong ch. 5), Feynman’s ratchet.
// Deliberate omissions: probability theory itself (CLT, LLN → prob), binary phase diagrams and
//   solution chemistry beyond colligative properties (→ pchem), nonequilibrium fluctuation theorems
//   (Jarzynski, Crooks) and the Kosterlitz–Thouless transition (not covered by the references),
//   hydrodynamics from the Boltzmann equation (→ fluid), the Saha equation (→ astro).
